      "message": "[warning] Line 192: 🟡 `emitConversationRemoved()` is now fired unconditionally right after `perform(.blockContact, ...)`, which decouples navigation from action completion. If contact removal/blocking becomes asynchronous (or starts reporting failures), UI will still navigate away as if removal succeeded. Prefer restoring the completion callback (`perform(..., completion: { [weak self] in self?.emitConversationRemoved() })`) so state transition happens only after the destructive action finishes.",
